.El
.Sh BUILD OPTIONS
.Nm
builds with Zig 0.17.0 or later, whose bundled Clang
compiles the C sources; GCC is not supported:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zig build -Doptimize=fast
.Ed
.Pp
The build installs into
.Pa zig-out/ :
.Pa lib/libxft.a
.Pq Pa lib/xft.lib No on Windows
and the headers under
.Pa include/xft/ .
On Linux it also installs
.Pa lib/libxft-perf.a
and
.Pa lib/libxft-tailor.a ,
see
.Sx PERF AND TAILOR .
Zig consumers link the
.Ql xft
artifact of the dependency, which carries the headers, the Windows import
libraries, and on Linux
.Nm perf
and
.Nm tailor .
On Linux every build adds
.Fl fstack-clash-protection
where Clang supports it, which excludes arm and mips.
.Bl -tag -width "-Dfast-math"
.It Fl Doptimize
.Ql debug ,
.Ql safe ,
.Ql fast
or
.Ql small .
.Ql fast
and
.Ql safe
also add
.Fl O3 .
Default
.Ql debug .
.It Fl Dtarget
The target triple, such as
.Ql x86_64-linux
or
.Ql x86_64-windows-gnu .
Linux targets other than x86_64 and aarch64, such as
.Ql x86-linux-gnu
or
.Ql arm-linux-gnueabihf ,
need
.Fl Duse-libc .
On 32-bit targets the library calls compiler-rt for 64-bit division;
executables built by Zig link it automatically.
Default the host.
.It Fl Dcpu
The CPU model and features, such as
.Ql native ,
.Ql baseline
or
.Ql x86_64_v3 .
Every ISA path in
.Nm
follows it.
Default
.Ql native .
.It Fl Duse-libc
Build against a libc instead of freestanding.
Threads go through the C library's pthreads; glibc older than 2.34 keeps
them in
.Pa libpthread ,
which executables built by Zig link automatically and which needs
.Fl lpthread
when linking the archive by hand.
Default off.
.It Fl Dsanitize
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and stack checks; Zig ships no AddressSanitizer
runtime.
Requires
.Fl Duse-libc
and disables LTO.
Zig rejects the stack checks on 32-bit x86, so a sanitized build, and with it
.Fl Dtests ,
does not build there.
Default off.
.It Fl Dlto
Full link-time optimization.
Default off.
.It Fl Dfast-math
Compile with
.Fl ffast-math .
Default off.
.It Fl Dllc
Last level cache size in bytes, defining
.Dv XFT_LLC_SIZE ,
above which
.Fn xft_memcpy
and
.Fn xft_memset
switch to non-temporal stores.
Default 16777216.
.It Fl Dtests
Build the unit tests, always sanitized, and the thread tests against a
freestanding build, which creates threads with
.Xr clone 2 .
The
.Cm test
step runs both, and
.Cm freestanding-thread-tests
runs only the thread tests.
.It Fl Dfuzz
Build the fuzz targets and the
.Cm fuzz
step that runs them.
Requires
.Fl Dsanitize
and
.Fl Duse-libc .
.It Fl Dbenches
Build the benchmarks and the
.Cm run-bench
step that runs them.
Requires
.Fl Doptimize=fast ,
no
.Fl Dsanitize ,
and Linux.
.It Fl Dbootstrap
Build the library without the xid module, build
.Nm gentable ,
and regenerate its table from
.Pa DerivedCoreProperties.txt
in the source root.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl Dtests .
See
.Xr xft_xid 3 .
.El
.Pp
Warnings are always errors.
.Sh PERF AND TAILOR
On Linux,
.Nm
builds two more libraries on top of
.Xr perf_event_open 2 ,
compiled with the same flavor as the library itself:
.Bl -tag -width "tailor"
.It Nm perf
.In xft/perf.h :
hardware and software performance counter groups, sampling, and CPU
pinning.
.It Nm tailor
.In xft/tailor.h :
the benchmark harness used by
.Pa bench/ ,
built on
.Nm perf .
.El
.Pp
Both link
.Nm
and are linked by it in the Zig build.
Linking the archives by hand, they go before
.Nm :
.Fl lxft-tailor Fl lxft-perf Fl lxft .
They are not built for Windows.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft.h>

void	xft_main(const t_any *__restrict__ const sp)
{
	(void)sp;
	xft_exit_process(0);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_alloc 3 ,
.Xr xft_io 3 ,
.Xr xft_rt 3 ,
.Xr xft_xid 3
